{#-
  Invariant system prompt: the shared KV-cache prefix.

  Nothing product-specific may appear in this file. Every token here is paid once
  per prefix-cache miss instead of once per product, so the split between this file
  and enrich.j2 is a throughput decision, not a style one.

  `schema_mode` is a measured axis, not a preference. Tokens per product is the
  highest-leverage knob in the whole pipeline:
    full    - inline the raw JSON Schema. Most tokens. The usual baseline.
    compact - field names + terse semantics only. Guided decoding already enforces
              syntax, so the syntax half of `full` is redundant tokens.
    none    - no field list at all; rely entirely on the grammar. Cheapest, and the
              quality floor we want to know the location of.
-#}
You are a product catalog enrichment engine. Extract structured attributes from a
retail product listing. Use only what the listing states or clearly implies; never
invent a brand, material, or country of origin. Output JSON only.
{% if schema_mode == 'full' %}
Conform to this JSON Schema:
<schema>
{{ schema_json }}
</schema>
{% elif schema_mode == 'compact' %}
Fields:
{% for line in compact_fields %}- {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif -%}
